## 2. ENGLISH VERSION

### 2.1. Intellectual Property Notice
The software product "Architect of History" (Anno Domini 1180), including all of its components, is protected by international copyright laws, treaties, and intellectual property conventions. All exclusive rights, title, and interest belong solely to the author and copyright holder (Melok90).

### 2.2. Protected Assets
Copyright protection strictly covers, without limitation:
1. **Narrative & Lore:** Original screenplay, chapters, dialogue, character profiles (Brother Luke, Abbot Odo, Prior Guillaume, Novice Thomas, Simon, Brother Raymond), secret relics, lore documentation, worldbuilding, and random event storylines.
2. **Art & Visual Design (Trade Dress):** Woodcut engravings, character portraits, custom SVG iconography (`ICONS`), medieval manuscript user interface, layout, typography, and visual assets.
3. **Software & Audio:** All source code (HTML, CSS, JavaScript), game logic, and procedural Web Audio API synthesis algorithms.
4. **Branding:** The project name "Architect of History" / "Архитектор Истории", logos, and associated marks.

### 2.3. Permitted Use
You are permitted to play the game for personal, non-commercial entertainment and create gameplay videos, streams, or reviews provided that proper attribution and a link to the official repository (`https://github.com/Melok90/architect-history`) are included.

### 2.4. Prohibitions
Without prior explicit written authorization from the copyright holder, you may NOT:
- Copy, clone, redistribute, rehost, sublicense, or sell the source code, narrative, artwork, or game mechanics;
- Create derivative works or games using the characters, universe, or distinctive trade dress;
- Use any assets, texts, or code for training artificial intelligence or machine learning models;
- Remove or alter any copyright notices, watermarks, or authorship links.

